IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-fixtures`
IMPORT `ucta-part3`

-- Tests for ucta-part3.l4 (sections 26 to 30).  Every expected value is written from the text.
-- `mk part3` takes: places of business in different States; goods in the course of carriage between
-- States; offer and acceptance in different States; delivery to another State; Singapore law only by
-- choice; sea carriage of a passenger; the Minister's order prescribes it; authorised by an
-- instrument; that instrument; made to comply with an international agreement; not more
-- restrictive than the agreement; date contract made; date loss suffered; s 5 Civil Law Act 1909.

§ `s 26 - international supply contracts`

-- s 26(3)(a) and (b) met, s 26(4)(a) met (goods carried between States): described.
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(4)(b) alone: the acts constituting offer and acceptance were done in different States.
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(4)(c) alone: delivery to a State other than the one where those acts were done.
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(3)(a): a contract under which possession of goods passes also satisfies (a): hire-purchase and other goods contracts.
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A hire-purchase agreement` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A contract, not of sale of goods or hire-purchase, under which possession or ownership of goods passes` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(4): "only if either (a), (b) or (c)": none is met, so the contract is not within subsection (3).
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(3)(b): the parties' places of business are in the same State, so the description is not met although (4)(a) is.
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(3)(a): a contract of services (no goods pass) is not described, even if the parties are in different States.
#ASSERT `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 26(1): "The limits imposed by this Act ... do not apply to liability arising under such a contract".
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the limits imposed by this Act on excluding or restricting liability apply to liability under the contract` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not an international supply contract: subsection (1) does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the limits imposed by this Act on excluding or restricting liability apply to liability under the contract` `A contract of sale of goods` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 26(2): "The terms of such a contract are not subject to any requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4".
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the terms of the contract are subject to a requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the terms of the contract are subject to a requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 27 - choice of law clauses`

-- s 27(1): Singapore law only by choice of the parties: sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 operate as part of the proper law` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Singapore law for another reason: subsection (1) does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 operate as part of the proper law` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 27(2): no term applying foreign law, so the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a): the term appears to the court to have been imposed to evade this Act.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b): a party dealt as consumer, was then habitually resident in Singapore, and the essential steps were taken there.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) fails on residence; (a) fails: neither limb, so the "where" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) fails on the essential steps; (a) fails.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) fails because no party dealt as consumer; (a) fails.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) is a judgment of the court not yet made and (b) fails: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Whether a party dealt as consumer is not known, the other facts of (b) are met, (a) fails: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 28 - sea carriage of passengers`

-- s 28(1): applies to a contract for carriage by sea of a passenger.
#ASSERT `s 28(1) section 28 applies to the contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(1) section 28 applies to the contract` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 28(2): "A person is not precluded by this Act from excluding or restricting liability ... as may be prescribed by order": the order prescribes it.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) this Act precludes the person from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The order does not prescribe this circumstance and term.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) this Act precludes the person from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister's order is not among the sources and the person cannot say.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) this Act precludes the person from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a contract for the carriage by sea of a passenger.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) this Act precludes the person from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 29 - saving for other relevant legislation`

-- s 29(3): "enactment means any legislation (including subsidiary legislation) of Singapore and any instrument having effect by virtue of such legislation".
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` `Legislation of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` `Subsidiary legislation of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` `An instrument having effect by virtue of legislation of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` `Something else` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 29(3): "competent authority means any court, arbitrator or arbiter, Government department or public authority".
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` `A court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` `An arbitrator or arbiter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` `A Government department` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` `A public authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` `Another body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 29(3): "statutory means conferred by an enactment".
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the jurisdiction or function is statutory` `Legislation of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the jurisdiction or function is statutory` `Something else` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 29(1)(a): a provision authorised by the express terms of an enactment.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE `Legislation of Singapore` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) fails because the instrument is not an enactment.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): made with a view to compliance with an international agreement and not more restrictive than it contemplates.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) fails: the provision operates more restrictively than the agreement contemplates.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Neither (a) nor (b): the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 29(2): incorporated or approved by a competent authority acting in the exercise of a statutory function, and not its own contract.
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` TRUE `A court` `Legislation of Singapore` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` TRUE `A Government department` `Subsidiary legislation of Singapore` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The competent authority is itself a party to the contract.
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` TRUE `A court` `Legislation of Singapore` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not incorporated or approved by it.
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` FALSE `A court` `Legislation of Singapore` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a competent authority.
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` TRUE `Another body` `Legislation of Singapore` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a statutory jurisdiction or function.
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` TRUE `A court` `Something else` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 30 - transitional`

-- s 30(2): contract made before 12 November 1993, and not applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 11 11 1993) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The loss was suffered before that day (contract made after).
#ASSERT `s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 11 11 1993) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Boundary: made on 12 November 1993 is not "before 12 November 1993".
#ASSERT `s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 12 11 1993) (Date 12 11 1993) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "except in so far as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909": the exception is met (QA).
#ASSERT `s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 11 11 1993) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Whether the 1909 Act applied is outside the sources.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 11 11 1993) (Date 1 3 2024) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A contract made after: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 1(2) - whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case`

#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `A contract of sale of goods` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
-- An international supply contract (s 26): out.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- Singapore law only by choice (s 27(1)): out.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- The Minister's order prescribes it (s 28(2)): out.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- Sea carriage of a passenger, order not known: cannot be told.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told`
-- Sea carriage of a passenger, the order does not prescribe it: no exception.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
-- A statutorily authorised provision (s 29(1)): out.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE `Legislation of Singapore` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- A 1992 contract, the 1909 Act not applicable (s 30(2)): out.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 1992) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- A 1992 contract, the 1909 Act question not answered: cannot be told.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 1992) (Date 1 3 2024) NOTHING) EQUALS `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told`

§ `Item 2 of the fix round: s 27(1) in its own words`

-- "Where the proper law of a contract is the law of Singapore only by choice of the parties ... sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law".
#ASSERT `s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "Where" is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): Singapore law is the proper law for another reason, so the subsection does not switch sections 2 to 7 off.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law` `an ordinary part 3` EQUALS JUST FALSE
